  {
   "id": 50,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    0,
    1300
   ],
   "size": [
    820,
    680
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 50,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 1 \u00b7 Your inputs\n**Mesh:** pick a GLB in **Load 3D**. **UV unwrap** gives it UVs:\n- `comfy_gpu`: fast, the default.\n- `xatlas`: slower; the developer says it often looks better, since better UVs = better texture.\n- `keep_existing`: your mesh already has clean UVs (Blender, Maya).\n\n**Big mesh? \"413 Request Entity Too Large\"** means the file is over ComfyUI's 100 MB upload limit. Either copy the GLB into `ComfyUI/input/3d/` and press **R**, or add `--max-upload-size 2048` to `Start ComfyUI.bat` and fully restart (EZi app too).\n\n**Reference image:** a front view of the object, ideally the image you generated the mesh from.\n**BiRefNet** removes the background, so any image works. Prepare is set to `mask_polarity = foreground` to match.\n\n**Text and logos** only come out clean if they are sharp in the reference, ideally on the front."
   ],
   "title": "Read me \u00b7 Inputs",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 51,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    880,
    1300
   ],
   "size": [
    400,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 51,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 2 \u00b7 GGUF models\n| File | Folder |\n|---|---|\n| `flux-2-klein-base-9b-Q4_0.gguf` (5.6 GB) | `models/diffusion_models` |\n| `Qwen3-8B-Q4_K_M.gguf` (~5 GB) | `models/text_encoders` |\n| `flux2-vae.safetensors` | `models/vae` |\n| UltraTex LoRAs + decoder | same as the fp8 workflows |\n| `birefnet.safetensors` | `models/background_removal` |\n\nKlein GGUF: `unsloth/FLUX.2-klein-base-9B-GGUF`. **Must be the BASE model.**\nQwen GGUF: `unsloth/Qwen3-8B-GGUF`. **Q4_K_M** because the text encoder only encodes an **empty prompt**, so a smaller quant costs practically nothing and saves VRAM. Have `Qwen3-8B-Q6_K.gguf`? Just pick it here.\nNeeds **ComfyUI-GGUF** (city96) for the two GGUF loaders."
   ],
   "title": "Read me \u00b7 Models",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 52,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1340,
    1300
   ],
   "size": [
    420,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 52,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 3 \u00b7 Prepare\nRenders the normal views and lines your reference up with the front camera.\n\n**Check the three previews before a long run:**\n- **Normal views:** your mesh from all sides.\n- **Aligned reference:** the object should fill the silhouette **edge to edge**.\n- **Aligned mask:** white object on black.\n\nSmall or shifted? Check `mask_polarity`: **foreground** for BiRefNet, **background** if you use Load Image's own MASK instead."
   ],
   "title": "Read me \u00b7 Prepare",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 53,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1820,
    1300
   ],
   "size": [
    820,
    620
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 53,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 4 \u00b7 Generate views\n**All quality and speed settings live on the two Generate nodes.**\n\n| Setting | Albedo | MR | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `view_resolution` | **1024** | 1024 | 6 GB: 1024 \u00b7 8 GB: up to 1536\u20132048 |\n| `view_count` | **12** | **6** | 12 = 6 + a guided 45\u00b0 pass |\n| `steps` | **4** | 4 | dev: 4 is enough, 8 is better |\n| `extra_angle_mode` | guided | \u2013 | 45\u00b0 pass starts from pass 1 |\n\n- **Same seed** on both Generate nodes.\n- **Steps are the speed lever.** Time scales with steps. Compare 4 / 8 / 25 on your asset and judge the back and sides, not just the front.\n- MR maps are low-detail, so **6 views** are enough there.\n- `tiled_decode` **on** for low VRAM."
   ],
   "title": "Read me \u00b7 Generate",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 54,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    2700,
    1300
   ],
   "size": [
    840,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 54,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 5 \u00b7 Bake & save\nBakes albedo and MR views onto the **one shared UV layout**. Saves to `output/ultratex/`:\n- textured **GLB** (+ Preview 3D)\n- **base color**, **roughness** and **metallic** maps as separate PNGs\n\n| Setting | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `texture_size` | 2048 (4096 for hero assets, same VRAM, slower bake) |\n| `fill_unseen` | on: estimates hidden areas (no new detail) |\n| `blend_mode` | detail_preserving |\n| `repair_mode` | normal_aware_surface |\n\nFaceted face? Try `normal_mode = preserve` vs `smooth` in Prepare."
   ],
   "title": "Read me \u00b7 Bake",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 55,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    0,
    -820
   ],
   "size": [
    1760,
    780
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 55,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# UltraTex \u00b7 Low VRAM (GGUF) \u00b7 6\u20138 GB GPUs\n**PixelArtistry** \u00b7 GGUF node pack by **MostAadTech** (UltraTex-ComfyUI-nodes, MIT) \u00b7 original nodes by **visualbruno** \u00b7 model by the **UltraTex** team\n\nThe same UltraTex texturing, rebuilt for small GPUs: a **Q4 GGUF** Klein base model, a Q4_K_M GGUF Qwen3 text encoder, sparse attention, tiled decoding and disk-backed caching.\n\n### Reported VRAM and speed (not measured by PixelArtistry yet)\n| Card | Setting | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6 GB GPU (community test) | 1024 | runs |\n| RTX 5050 Laptop 8 GB (MostAadTech) | 1536, 12 views | **6.8 GB** dedicated VRAM |\n| unknown card (community test) | 2048, 4 steps | ~6 min |\n\nSpeed depends a lot on your card: two 8 GB cards can differ several times over.\n\n### How to use\n1. **Group 1:** pick your GLB and your reference image.\n2. Press **Run**. First check the previews in group 3.\n3. Results in `output/ultratex/`, and the GLB in **Preview 3D**.\n\n### Requirements\n- **UltraTex-ComfyUI-nodes** by MostAadTech: github.com/Mstafa-awad/UltraTex-ComfyUI-nodes (built for commit `b98f4f4`; the pack changes often).\n- **ComfyUI-GGUF** by city96.\n- **Triton** (`triton-windows` on Windows). This pack has **no fallback** without it.\n- A recent ComfyUI (native MESH, Load 3D, BiRefNet nodes).\n- The original visualbruno pack is **not** required. Both packs can be installed side by side.\n\n### License\n- UltraTex code and nodes: MIT.\n- FLUX.2 Klein base 9B: FLUX Non-Commercial License v2.1. BFL claims no ownership of your outputs and allows using them for any purpose, including commercial, except training a competing model. Running the model itself is licensed for non-commercial use, so check https://bfl.ai/licensing before client or production work.\n"
   ],
   "title": "START HERE \u00b7 UltraTex Low VRAM (GGUF)",
   "color": "#223",
   "bgcolor": "#335"
  }
